    Refactor savestate transfers and fix controller/RAM issues (#216)
    
    * Refactor duplicated VRAM savestate transfers
    
    Consolidate the duplicated VDP1 and VDP2 active/passive VRAM save and load paths while preserving the existing state machine, transfer timing,
    port retention, and save-state layout.
    
    Keep WRAM, NVRAM, snapshot serialization, and restore sequencing unchanged.
    
    No functional changes intended.
    
    * Fix port B output register mapping in dpram
    
    Forward the port B output-register generic to the corresponding altsyncram parameter instead of incorrectly reusing the port A setting.
    
    Current SMS RAM instances use unregistered outputs on both ports, so their effective configuration remains unchanged.
    
    * Fix Master Tap TH edge detection
    
    Use the console-driven TH output for Master Tap timing and edge detection instead of the controller-returned TH input.
    
    The TH input/output paths were split in 2020, but the existing Master Tap logic continued monitoring the returned signal, which remains high for virtual USB controllers. As a result, console TH pulses could not
    advance the selected controller.
    
    Preserve the existing timeout, controller routing, and savestate behavior.

